<title>SINGAPORE: Indonesia allocates 258-263,000 bpd April crude.</title>
<headline>Indonesia allocates 258-263,000 bpd April crude.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's state-owned Pertamina has allocated about 257,800 to 262,800 barrels per day (bpd) of crude for export in April, down from the initial March allocation of 290,600 bpd, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The Minas allocation was 61,000 bpd, down from 94,300 in March.</p>
<p>Duri allocation was 70,700 bpd, up from 45,700 in March.  </p>
<p>The following allocations of Pertamina's key grades were made, industry sources said. Figures are in barrels per day:</p>
<p>		 April	 March</p>
<p>Minas	  61,000	94,300</p>
<p>Duri	   70,700	45,700</p>
<p>Cinta	  14,200	24,700</p>
<p>Widuri	 16,800	27,200</p>
<p>Arun	   30,700	24,200</p>
<p>Belida	 12,000	11,200</p>
<p>Bontang Mix  27,400	38,100</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3081)</p>
</text>
